# 28. Relationship to the Eight Conservation Bottlenecks

The science/data pillar also demonstrates that information problems rarely exist independently.

### Knowledge

Is the ecological condition understood?

### Diagnosis

Are its causes understood?

### Authority

Can someone legally respond?

### Capacity

Are resources and personnel available?

### Coordination

Can relevant institutions act together?

### Ecological

Does the system respond as expected?

### Allocation

Can competing uses be reconciled?

### Durability

Can gains and institutional capacity persist?

Science primarily addresses the first two.

But the information system becomes most valuable when it connects to all eight.

